course: dictionary
lesson: 1188
title: Blend words
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A blend is a new word made by joining parts of two other words. «Brunch» comes from «breakfast» and «lunch»: it takes the start of breakfast (br) and the end of lunch (unch). Blends often have letters from both words squashed together.
explain: Brunch means a meal eaten in the late morning instead of breakfast and lunch, often bigger than breakfast. People often have brunch at a café at the weekend, with pancakes, eggs or waffles.
explain: Other blends work the same way. «Smog» is smoke + fog, «motel» is motor + hotel, and «hangry» is hungry + angry. When you meet a new word, look for two words hiding inside it, then think about what both parts mean together.
fact: A blend is a new word made from parts of two words.
fact: «Brunch» means a late-morning meal instead of breakfast and lunch.
fact: «Smog» is smoke + fog.
fact: «Motel» is motor + hotel.
fact: «Hangry» is hungry + angry, and it is now in major dictionaries.
exercise: Which two words are blended to make «brunch»? | bread and munch | brunch and lunch | *breakfast and lunch | lunch and dinner
exercise: What does «brunch» mean? | *A meal eaten in the late morning, instead of breakfast and lunch | A very small snack before bed | A cup of tea eaten at lunchtime
exercise: Which blend word is made from smoke and fog? | *smog | hangry | motel
test: «Hangry» is a blend. Which two words make it? | happy and angry | hard and angry | *hungry and angry | hungry and anger
test: A café serves brunch at the weekend. When is brunch usually eaten? | Just before bed | Very early, before the sun is up | Late at night | *In the late morning
exam: Blend «motor» and «hotel». What new word do you make? | motohotel | smotor | *motel | hotor
